{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1121212-vampire-and-vision","id":1121212,"title":"Vampire and vision","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-27T00:02:43-07:00","id":1121212,"title":"Vampire and vision","content":"What if a human with vision problems that needed glasses were turned into a Vampire. Would that vampire has 20/20 vision?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1945-magicballz","name":"Magicballz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T00:29:14-07:00","id":1121217,"title":"","content":"Well there is a flaw for that.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T04:40:05-07:00","id":1121256,"title":"","content":"The beast usually fixes such problems to make the vampire a more perfect predator. But occasionally it fails to do so, and the resultant vampire needs glasses like a kine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T08:16:09-07:00","id":1121315,"title":"","content":"Flaws you had as a person stay. If you're in a wheelchair, you're in a wheelchair. If you have bad eyes, hope that you get Auspex. You are frozen in the moment of death. So, most clans are really careful about embracing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13654-davesknd","name":"Davesknd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T16:13:22-07:00","id":1121603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Davesknd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1121212-vampire-and-vision?p=1121315#post1121315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Flaws you had as a person stay. If you're in a wheelchair, you're in a wheelchair. If you have bad eyes, hope that you get Auspex. You are frozen in the moment of death. So, most clans are really careful about embracing.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not quite true. It usually fixes the throat wounds, for example, unless you take the flaw that you start wounded. It obviously adds fangs. Vampires aren't completely frozen in the moment of death. They are mutated slightly to make them better predators. Whether that includes fixing minor eyesight problems is random.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T16:30:59-07:00","id":1121611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1121212-vampire-and-vision?p=1121603#post1121603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not quite true. It usually fixes the throat wounds, for example, unless you take the flaw that you start wounded. It obviously adds fangs. Vampires aren't completely frozen in the moment of death. They are mutated slightly to make them better predators. Whether that includes fixing minor eyesight problems is random.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ok, they probably added that in V20, because Revised was pretty clear that you stay as you are when you died. Fangs and so on are supernatural (I think in the Malkavian clanbook, Netchurch even mentions that you can't see them on x-rays).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13654-davesknd","name":"Davesknd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T15:53:32-07:00","id":1124988,"title":"","content":"When you embrace someone, they get stronger physically and their body undergoes some small changes. Someone who can't walk MIGHT find themselves able to walk after the embrace, but they might not. Remember that Vitae isn't just a preservative, it *heals* in a way which shows that it cares about restoring things to their proper order. It reverses Vicissitude changes. It heals humans and animals. It closes small wounds through licking.<br /> <br /> So if someone has poor eyesight, they could rise with improved Perception and perfect eyes, or they could have the Flaw still and have to deal with it forever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T18:14:59-07:00","id":1125031,"title":"","content":"Exactly. Vitae is not embalming fluid, it's The Beast in liquid form. The Beast wants its shell to be an efficient predatory tool. So it fixes and mutates. It's not very smart, though, so screws up occasionally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T09:47:16-07:00","id":1125938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Davesknd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1121212-vampire-and-vision?p=1121611#post1121611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, they probably added that in V20, because Revised was pretty clear that you stay as you are when you died. Fangs and so on are supernatural (I think in the Malkavian clanbook, Netchurch even mentions that you can't see them on x-rays).</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that was in Revised as well - take a look at the permanent wound flaw that mentions a physical wound that is not healed by the Embrace is an anomaly. As the others have said, the Embrace is not exactly a precise process that has always the same result, but it does have a chance to fix things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T16:16:05-07:00","id":1126093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1121212-vampire-and-vision?p=1125938#post1125938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, that was in Revised as well - take a look at the permanent wound flaw that mentions a physical wound that is not healed by the Embrace is an anomaly. As the others have said, the Embrace is not exactly a precise process that has always the same result, but it does have a chance to fix things.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Looks like I was wrong. Thx for clearing it up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13654-davesknd","name":"Davesknd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T20:00:46-07:00","id":1142012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DAV20 Core Book p22 &quot;Physiognomy of the Dead&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your body, mine, all of us, are made of sin. It\u2019s not a thing to be ashamed of; it\u2019s simply what it is. What a human can do we can do better. We can run faster and see in the dark. For most of us, our bodies become more perfect visions of what we were as humans. No, not me, childe, but I am a special kind of sinner. No! You are a creature meant to steal virtue and arouse vice. You drink blood and tempt the holy with your strange secret powers and your allure.<br /> It\u2019s the cleanliness about you that\u2019s always thrown me. Even in my clan, don\u2019t our teeth straighten and grow so very white? I\u2019ve watched during the Embrace, watches as pox marks vanish and turn to baby-smooth skin, or even smoother. Once, I saw a lad who was struck by an affliction of the crown that left him bald as a friar, but didn\u2019t Damnation go and give him a head full of lovely hair. Didn\u2019t he just become a randy beast as a result? This is what I\u2019m saying! We\u2019re creatures made of sin rebuilt by the corruption of Caine to spread slowly but surely across all four corners of the earth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Modern day Vampire seems to not take quite the same outlook, but in general a lot of superficial flaws will be fixed by the embrace, skin tightens, some fat is lost, never have complexion issues again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":16927,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","user":"Illithid","date":". 09-19-2017, 11:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}